      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-17T20:07:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "@jiyong, does microdroid_manager know whether the the payload will be debuggable in any way?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 217,
        "startChar": 35,
        "endLine": 217,
        "endChar": 90
      },
      "revId": "04f232aadcc51677aeceefa549d69d32d5b1718c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c226b670_20202972",
        "filename": "microdroid_manager/src/main.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 217,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-18T05:06:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You can read the sysprop ro.boot.microdroid.debuggable to see if it\u0027s debuggable or not. (Note that it\u0027s part of bootconfig)",
      "parentUuid": "ce004f9b_e47e1897",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 217,
        "startChar": 35,
        "endLine": 217,
        "endChar": 90
      },
      "revId": "04f232aadcc51677aeceefa549d69d32d5b1718c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d88001b1_480f3efa",
        "filename": "microdroid_manager/src/main.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 217,
      "author": {
        "id": 1139038
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-18T17:23:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I also noticed another property `ro.boot.logd.enabled` and `ro.boot.adb.enabled` that sounds related to the debug level of the VM. How do these interact with each other?",
      "parentUuid": "c226b670_20202972",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 217,
        "startChar": 35,
        "endLine": 217,
        "endChar": 90
      },
      "revId": "04f232aadcc51677aeceefa549d69d32d5b1718c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "169bafcf_20ee54dd",
        "filename": "microdroid_manager/src/main.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 217,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-18T17:45:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The three sysprops controls different aspects of the debuggability. ro.boot.microdroid.debuggable controls if rooting is allowed or not. logd.enabled and adbd.enabled control logd and adbd respectively. See bootconfig.{normal,app_debuggable,full_debuggable} to see how they are set for the three debug modes we have.\n\nSince DICE defines only two debug modes–\"Not configured\" and \"Recovery\" can be ignored here I think–, we have to map app_debuggable to either Debug or Normal. When I suggested using ro.boot.microdroid.debuggable, I wanted to map app_debuggable to Normal because the sysprop is 0 in both bootconfig.normal and bootconfig.app_debuggable.\n\nIf you want to make only bootconfig.normal as Normal, then we could use the other two sysprops.\n\nOr, we could add a new sysprop like ro.boot.microdroid.debug_mode and set androidboot.microdroid.debug_mode to either normal, app_only, or full in the three bootconfig files. Then inside microdroid we set DICE debug mode as normal only when the sysprop is set to \"normal\".",
      "parentUuid": "d88001b1_480f3efa",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 217,
        "startChar": 35,
        "endLine": 217,
        "endChar": 90
      },
      "revId": "04f232aadcc51677aeceefa549d69d32d5b1718c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a9010fda_2d98f219",
        "filename": "microdroid_manager/src/main.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 217,
      "author": {
        "id": 1139038
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-18T18:19:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Perhaps u-boot should set its mode to Debug when based on androidboot.microdroid.debuggable, since that makes microdroid rootable.\n\nWhether logging and adb affect the payload sounds like a policy choice. Thinking how you have to enable adb in the debug settings on a physical device is something that makes me wonder whether adb on your payload should be something to worry about. Gaining shell is often something you don\u0027t want to happen, even if you don\u0027t yet have root.",
      "parentUuid": "169bafcf_20ee54dd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 217,
        "startChar": 35,
        "endLine": 217,
        "endChar": 90
      },
      "revId": "04f232aadcc51677aeceefa549d69d32d5b1718c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
